==Trivia==  
*The idea of card games originated from China during the ninth century AD, as a result of the usage of woodblock printing technology. Later, it passed towards the Middle East and Europe and took many forms.
*{{Rarity|Epic}} Cards can only be requested once every Sunday; {{Rarity|Legendary}} and {{Rarity|Champion}} Cards cannot be donated or requested.
*In the Japanese language setting, {{Rarity|Epic}} Cards are called Super Rare Cards while {{Rarity|Legendary}} Cards are called Ultra Rare Cards, the terms often used in card collection games. In the Korean language setting, {{Rarity|Epic}} Cards are called Heroic Cards.
*Despite Epic Chests only being able to give {{Rarity|Epic}} Cards, an Epic Chest may not give any {{Rarity|Epic}} Cards. This can happen if the player does not have any {{Rarity|Epic}} Cards unlocked and this Chest is opened in Arenas where no {{Rarity|Epic}} Cards can be unlocked. It can also happen with {{Rarity|Legendary}} Chests.
*Even though a deck can only have 1 {{Rarity|Champion}} Card at a time, there have been cases of multiple {{Rarity|Champion}} Cards within a deck. In these scenarios, using the ability would use it for both {{Rarity|Champion}} Cards.

